  "problem": "Find, **in radians**, the argument of $z=-8-5\\text{i}.$ Round your final answer to **two decimal places**.\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$arg\u2061(z)\u2248$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13929099/assets/c598c3b872cd2c4b3af08d8b2dbaf6a79512fe382473320feb526f31e5ece246.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the third quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\pi <arg\u2061(z)<\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the negative real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =arctan\\,(\\frac{5}{8})=0.558\\,599\u2026\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg\u2061(z)=\\pi +0.558\\,599\u2026\u22483.70,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
